  "description": "TPO 15 Lansdowne Gardens and 12 Guildford Road 1969, confirmed 1970:  T22 Horse Chestnut\rLocation: Rear garden adjacent to the boundary wall at 49 Lansdowne Gardens\rProposed tree works: Fell to ground level.\rReason: Poor physiological and structural condition and ongoing conflict with the adjacent boundary wall as set out in the submitted arboricultural and structural reports.\rReplacement planting proposed: Plant 2 replacement trees comprising 1 × Ginkgo biloba and 1 × Liriodendron tulipifera, both 10 to 12 cm Select Standards.\rCouncil Note:\rThe Council notes the proposal to plant 2 replacement trees comprising 1 x Ginkgo biloba and 1 x Liriodendron tulipifera. Only 1 replacement tree can be secured by condition as the direct replacement for the protected tree. Accordingly, 1 x Liriodendron tulipifera will be secured by condition, with planting required during the next planting season (September 2026 to March 2027) unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Council\r"
